    "output_text": "```python\ndef binary_search(sorted_list: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Perform binary search on a sorted list of integers.\n    \n    Args:\n        sorted_list: A list of integers sorted in ascending order.\n        target: The integer value to search for.\n        \n    Returns:\n        The index of the target in the list if found, otherwise -1.\n        \n    Time Complexity: O(log n), where n is the length of the list.\n    Space Complexity: O(1) for the iterative implementation.\n    \"\"\"\n    left: int = 0\n    right: int = len(sorted_list) - 1\n    \n    while left <= right:\n        mid: int = left + (right - left) // 2\n        mid_value: int = sorted_list[mid]\n        \n        if mid_value == target:\n            return mid\n        elif mid_value < target:\n            left = mid + 1\n        else:\n            right = mid - 1\n    \n    return -1\n```",
